Subject: [PATCH] compositor: destroy the clients before clearing the window state on exit

CCompositor::cleanup() clears the workspace/window/layer state before
wl_display_destroy_clients(). After that, a window's last strong reference
is the render pass of the last frame (CSurfacePassElement's PHLWINDOW). The
first client to be destroyed unmaps its window, whose snapshot's
beginRender() clears the pass, and every other window is freed without
unmapWindow(). ~CWindow() doesn't remove the layout target, so dwindle and
master keep expired nodes, and master crashes in calculateWorkspace()
(dwindle is guarded since 338bdbb3). Destroying the clients first, while the
state still exists, makes every window leave its layout through the normal
unmap path.

diff --git a/src/Compositor.cpp b/src/Compositor.cpp
index 122d8774..de87e046 100644
--- a/src/Compositor.cpp
+++ b/src/Compositor.cpp
@@ -589,6 +589,14 @@ void CCompositor::cleanup() {
     // still in a normal working state.
     g_pPluginSystem->unloadAllPlugins();
 
+    // destroy the clients while the windows, workspaces and monitors still exist, so that every
+    // window leaves its layout the normal way (unmap / destroy). With the window state cleared first,
+    // a window's last reference is the last frame's render pass, which the first unmap's snapshot
+    // clears: the other windows are then freed without an unmap, and their layout nodes expire.
+    g_pXWayland.reset();
+
+    wl_display_destroy_clients(g_pCompositor->m_wlDisplay);
+
     State::Workspace::state()->clear();
     Desktop::windowState()->clear();
     Desktop::layerState()->clear();
@@ -599,10 +607,6 @@ void CCompositor::cleanup() {
         g_pHyprOpenGL->destroyMonitorResources(m);
     }
 
-    g_pXWayland.reset();
-
-    wl_display_destroy_clients(g_pCompositor->m_wlDisplay);
-
     State::monitorState()->finish();
     State::fallbackState().reset();
     State::monitorState().reset();
